{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/pulls/805","id":3511012455,"node_id":"PR_kwDOALhqyM7RRcxn","html_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/805","diff_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/805.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/805.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/805","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/pulls/805/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/pulls/805/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/issues/805/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/hynek/structlog/statuses/7d7708fdf39061b6f7515c13ed0404a9bc05fb33","number":805,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Fix thread name CallsiteParameterAdder in async methods (issue #710)","user":{"login":"BlocksecPHD","id":118347763,"node_id":"U_kgDOBw3X8w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118347763?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD","html_url":"https://github.com/BlocksecPHD","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BlocksecPHD/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Problem\n\nWhen using async logging methods (`.ainfo()`, etc.), the `CallsiteParameterAdder` processor was collecting thread information from the executor thread pool instead of the caller's thread. This caused `thread_name` to show 'asyncio_0' instead of the actual caller thread like 'MainThread'.\n\n## Solution\n\nThis fix captures thread info (thread_id and thread_name) **before** passing control to the executor thread, storing it in a contextvar (`_ASYNC_CALLING_THREAD`) that is copied along with the calling stack frame. The processor then uses this captured thread info when available.\n\n## Changes\n\n1. **contextvars.py**: Added `_ASYNC_CALLING_THREAD` contextvar to store captured thread info\n2. **_native.py**: Updated async methods to capture thread info before executor\n3. **stdlib.py**: Updated async methods in both `BoundLogger` and `AsyncBoundLogger` to capture thread info\n4. **processors.py**: Updated `_get_callsite_thread` and `_get_callsite_thread_name` to use captured info from contextvar\n5. **tests**: Added tests to verify thread info is correctly captured in async context\n\n## Testing\n\nAll tests pass:\n- Native async tests\n- Stdlib async tests  \n- AsyncBoundLogger tests\n- Existing processor tests\n\n## Example Output\n\nBefore fix:\n```\nthread_name=asyncio_0  # Wrong - executor thread\n```\n\nAfter fix:\n```\nthread_name=MainThread  # Correct - caller's thread\n```\n\nFixes #710","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-04-09T22:17:33Z","updated_at":"2026-05-10T16:13:48Z","closed_at":"2026-05-10T16:13:48Z","merged_at":"2026-05-10T16:13:48Z","merge_commit_sha":"ba04ac275291ea1754aba24643d17cb8e5638c66","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"BlocksecPHD:fix-async-thread-info-710","ref":"fix-async-thread-info-710","repo":{"id":1206409657,"node_id":"R_kgDOR-hZuQ","name":"structlog","full_name":"BlocksecPHD/structlog","owner":{"login":"BlocksecPHD","id":118347763,"node_id":"U_kgDOBw3X8w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuserconte